cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use HuePrint, its probe batteries, or its empirical cloud response datasets, please cite this work."
title: "Talk Is Cheap, Show Me Your Colors: Low-Budget Consistency Auditing for Aggregated LLM Services"
type: article
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-18"
license: CC-BY-4.0
authors:
  - family-names: He
    given-names: Xiguan
    affiliation: "College of Information, Yunnan University of Chinese Medicine, Kunming 650500, China"
    email: kirarin@kirarin.dev
keywords:
  - large language models
  - model-as-a-service
  - service-level monitoring
  - API brokerage
  - behavioral consistency
  - energy statistics
abstract: >-
  Aggregated large language model services expose declared model identifiers while abstracting the backend
  configurations that fulfill client requests. We present HuePrint, a lightweight framework that audits brokered
  endpoint consistency via short structured color elicitation and continuous geometric distribution comparison without
  model weights or token probabilities. Across 34,528 cloud responses spanning 56 endpoints and 12 backends, HuePrint
  lowers 30-call-per-side equal error rates from 4.52-5.23 to 0.94-1.00 percent on the development cohort and from
  6.25-8.04 to 3.49-5.00 percent across 20 locked endpoints, reaching zero at moderate depth. Continuous and
  multi-scale RGB distances halve shallow-census error vs. exact-hex divergence (5.36 vs. 10.71 percent), cut
  cross-provider error from 16.67 to 5.93 percent, retain zero ranking error across three-week and cross-gateway checks
  where equality tests reject up to 42.86 percent of genuine pairs, and bound numerical perturbations.
